WEBVTT


00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:46.403
[HOOFBEATS]


00:01:19.061 --> 00:01:22.439
Randall, I'm afraid I gotta take
two of your boys back into town with me.


00:01:22.606 --> 00:01:25.317
You're outside your jurisdiction, marshaI.


00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:27.819
And you're trespassing on my land.


00:01:27.986 --> 00:01:31.823
They murdered that fellow from Chicago,
and then they raped and killed his wife.


00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.867
I'm taking them in.


00:01:37.537 --> 00:01:38.914
No.


00:01:39.081 --> 00:01:40.582
I can't spare them.


00:01:54.054 --> 00:01:57.057
Them two on the end. Cut them out.


00:01:59.893 --> 00:02:01.561
Do like I tell you.


00:02:59.536 --> 00:03:03.540
<i>HITCH: Like my father, I'd been West Point,
and I was good at soldiering.</i>


00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:07.377
<i>But soldiering didn't allow
for much expansion of the soul.</i>


00:03:07.544 --> 00:03:11.214
<i>So after the War Between the States
and a year of fighting Indians...</i>


00:03:11.381 --> 00:03:16.178
<i>...I turned in my commission and rode away
to see how much I could expand it.</i>


00:03:17.054 --> 00:03:20.182
<i>First time I met Virgil Cole
was when I and my eight-gauge...</i>


00:03:20.349 --> 00:03:22.476
<i>...backed him up in a showdown
he was having...</i>


00:03:22.643 --> 00:03:24.770
<i>...with some drunken mountain men.</i>


00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:27.898
<i>Virgil asked me on the spot
if I'd care to partner up with him...</i>


00:03:28.106 --> 00:03:30.317
<i>...and his peacekeeping business.</i>


00:03:30.484 --> 00:03:34.780
<i>Which is why I was with him now,
and why I still carry the eight-gauge.</i>


00:03:36.156 --> 00:03:39.826
<i>We'd been keeping the peace together
for the last dozen years or so.</i>


00:03:40.327 --> 00:03:43.538
<i>And as we looked down
on a town called Appaloosa...</i>


00:03:43.705 --> 00:03:46.416
<i>...I had no reason to doubt
that we'd be doing just that...</i>


00:03:46.583 --> 00:03:48.877
<i>...for the foreseeable future.</i>


00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:54.549
<i>But life has a way of making the foreseeable
that which never happens...</i>


00:03:54.716 --> 00:03:59.346
<i>...and the unforeseeable
that which your life becomes.</i>


00:04:21.451 --> 00:04:24.621
The black hat. Must be Cole.


00:04:28.625 --> 00:04:30.252
They're here.


00:04:34.381 --> 00:04:35.882
Howdy.


00:04:38.176 --> 00:04:41.054
RAINES: Jack Bell and his deputies
went up to Bragg's place...


00:04:41.221 --> 00:04:43.640
...to arrest the men
that murdered Clayton Poston...


00:04:43.807 --> 00:04:45.392
...and raped and killed his wife.


00:04:45.559 --> 00:04:49.438
And Jack Bell and his deputies
were never seen again.


00:04:49.605 --> 00:04:53.567
I knew Jack Bell. He was a good man.


00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.569
HITCH:
This fella, Bragg...


00:04:56.695 --> 00:04:58.030
...what's his story?


00:04:58.196 --> 00:04:59.906
He says he's from New York City.


00:05:00.073 --> 00:05:04.453
Claims that he worked with Chester Arthur
in the customs office up there.


00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.788
Chester Arthur,
President of the United States?


00:05:06.955 --> 00:05:09.207
RAINES:
That's what Bragg claims.


00:05:09.374 --> 00:05:10.918
What the hell's he doing out here?


00:05:11.084 --> 00:05:12.794
- He's after the copper fields.
- EarI.


00:05:12.961 --> 00:05:14.588
- What?
- Let Abner speak, please.


00:05:14.755 --> 00:05:16.298
He is speaking.


00:05:18.216 --> 00:05:22.554
The mines shut down back in '75
because of the Apache problem.


00:05:22.763 --> 00:05:23.889
We finally made a deaI...


00:05:24.097 --> 00:05:27.142
...with a company out of Chicago
to get the operation going again.


00:05:27.309 --> 00:05:28.393
A fair deaI, mind you.


00:05:28.602 --> 00:05:31.229
Then this murdering scoundreI
turns up and-


00:05:31.396 --> 00:05:32.731
- PhiI.
- What?


00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:36.068
Our investors pulled out
right after the killings.


00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:39.404
Bragg and his men
have got us all running scared.


00:05:39.613 --> 00:05:43.033
They buy supplies in my store
and they don't pay for them.


00:05:43.492 --> 00:05:44.660
They harass our women.


00:05:44.826 --> 00:05:47.496
They use horses from the livery
and don't bring them back.


00:05:47.663 --> 00:05:50.082
They eat and drink whatever they like
and never pay.


00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:54.586
They've been living off of us
like coyotes live off a buffalo carcass.


00:05:54.795 --> 00:05:57.631
Everything that eats meat
likes a dead buffalo.


00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.681
Mr. Cole, Mr. Hitch...


00:06:06.807 --> 00:06:10.686
...we want our town back,
and we are ready to pay your price.


00:06:12.813 --> 00:06:14.606
What do you allow, Everett?


00:06:16.817 --> 00:06:19.444
- What we do.
- It is, ain't it?


00:06:20.946 --> 00:06:22.823
Then you'll do it?


00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:26.201
- Sure.
- Oh, thank God.


00:06:26.368 --> 00:06:27.953
Mr. Cole and I will do the gun work...


00:06:28.161 --> 00:06:31.206
...but we're gonna button the town up
tighter than a nun's corset.


00:06:31.373 --> 00:06:33.208
We need you to make laws
we can enforce.


00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:34.710
We got laws.


00:06:34.876 --> 00:06:39.381
HITCH: You're gonna have more.
We need a lot of laws to make it all legaI.


00:06:39.673 --> 00:06:44.011
Well, sure. I mean, if it seems reasonable,
we'll just put them right into the bylaws.


00:06:44.177 --> 00:06:46.930
- No.
- No what?


00:06:49.224 --> 00:06:51.226
[MEN SHOUTING
INDISTINCTLY IN DISTANCE]


00:06:56.607 --> 00:07:00.527
It basically states
that whatever Mr. Cole says is law.


00:07:00.902 --> 00:07:04.072
- This means you'd be running the town.
- It does.


00:07:04.239 --> 00:07:06.408
We can't have that.


00:07:06.783 --> 00:07:10.662
I mean, you're asking us, so to speak,
to turn the town over to you.


00:07:10.871 --> 00:07:13.165
Far as I can see,
you're gonna turn it over anyway.


00:07:13.373 --> 00:07:15.250
- Us or Bragg.
- Mr. Raines.


00:07:15.417 --> 00:07:16.919
RAINES:
Not now, Tilda.


00:07:17.085 --> 00:07:18.921
- Trouble in the bar, Mr. Raines.
- Tilda.


00:07:19.087 --> 00:07:21.340
- It's Mr. Bragg's men.
OLSON: Oh, Jesus, God.


00:07:21.506 --> 00:07:24.051
There's four of them. They have guns.


00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:31.224
HITCH: Space for your signature
down at the bottom, gentlemen.


00:07:31.475 --> 00:07:32.976
Oh, for God's sake, give me that.


00:07:36.897 --> 00:07:38.398
So...


00:07:47.574 --> 00:07:49.368
Sign the damn thing, Abner...


00:07:49.576 --> 00:07:52.412
...so these men can do
what they came here to do.


00:08:18.939 --> 00:08:21.525
BRONC:
You piss like a mare, Chalk.


00:08:22.234 --> 00:08:25.070
Fat, give me another one.


00:08:26.238 --> 00:08:27.614
[LAUGHING]


00:08:33.287 --> 00:08:34.913
Button them up.


00:08:38.625 --> 00:08:42.129
- Who the fuck are you?
- VirgiI Cole.


00:08:42.296 --> 00:08:44.298
VirgiI Cole?


00:08:45.757 --> 00:08:47.426
No shit.


00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:51.638
Hey, Chalk,
VirgiI Cole wants us to button up.


00:08:53.473 --> 00:08:57.603
Step a little closer, VirgiI Cole,
and I'll piss in your pocket.


00:08:58.604 --> 00:09:02.482
Fellas, I'm the new city marshaI.
Put it away or lose it.


00:09:02.649 --> 00:09:06.612
- Hey, Bronc, they got a new city marshaI.
- Put your little contraptions away.


00:09:06.778 --> 00:09:10.574
I'm gonna walk you down to the jailhouse.
I don't wanna spook the horses.


00:09:20.375 --> 00:09:22.878
You ain't walking us nowhere, VirgiI Cole.


00:09:23.754 --> 00:09:27.633
You pull on me, either one of you...


00:09:28.008 --> 00:09:29.009
...I'll kill you both.


00:09:31.386 --> 00:09:33.388
Bullshit.


00:09:39.102 --> 00:09:42.814
I ain't shooting, mister. I ain't shooting.


00:09:46.526 --> 00:09:48.487
HITCH:
Give me your gun.


00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:07.839
I warned them.


00:10:41.999 --> 00:10:44.585
- MarshaI.
- Morning, Mr. Olson.


00:10:44.751 --> 00:10:48.046
Bragg and his men, some of them
were at the jaiI looking for you, sir.


00:10:48.213 --> 00:10:49.923
Well, I ain't at the jaiI.


00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:52.801
Yes, I can see that.


00:10:54.761 --> 00:10:58.223
Get a better view of what's going on
sitting right here, don't we, Everett?


00:10:58.557 --> 00:10:59.891
HITCH:
Mm-hm.


00:11:00.225 --> 00:11:01.935
What should we do?


00:11:02.644 --> 00:11:05.897
- About what?
- Well, about Bragg and his men.


00:11:06.106 --> 00:11:07.816
Don't do nothing, PhiI.


00:11:07.983 --> 00:11:09.735
Oh, my God.


00:11:29.796 --> 00:11:31.590
My name's Randall Bragg.


00:11:31.757 --> 00:11:33.425
VirgiI Cole.


00:11:35.344 --> 00:11:37.846
I know who you are.


00:11:41.141 --> 00:11:42.517
We need to talk.


00:11:42.684 --> 00:11:44.645
COLE:
The only thing I need from you...


00:11:45.646 --> 00:11:48.065
...is what happened to Jack Bell.


00:11:48.357 --> 00:11:50.525
Can't help you there, marshaI.


00:11:53.278 --> 00:11:55.739
I see the fellow with the shotgun there.


00:11:55.906 --> 00:11:57.699
Eight-gauge.


00:11:59.159 --> 00:12:01.703
Good idea, spreading out like that.


00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:03.455
It is.


00:12:09.253 --> 00:12:12.756
- You a drinking man, marshaI?
- Not so much.


00:12:13.215 --> 00:12:15.717
And, uh, Mr. Eight-Gauge over there?


00:12:15.884 --> 00:12:17.886
COLE:
Mr. Everett Hitch.


00:12:18.679 --> 00:12:20.639
BRAGG:
You a drinking man, Everett?


00:12:20.806 --> 00:12:22.766
Not so much.


00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:26.979
Hard to like a man
who doesn't drink a little.


00:12:27.187 --> 00:12:29.398
But not impossible.


00:12:30.732 --> 00:12:33.277
Well, we'll see.


00:12:38.699 --> 00:12:41.994
- You shot three of my men.
- Matter of fact, I only shot two.


00:12:42.202 --> 00:12:43.662
Mr. Hitch shot the other one.


00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:48.292
Point is, I can't have my hands
coming in here and you boys shooting them.


00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.085
I can see how you'd feeI that way.


00:12:50.252 --> 00:12:53.130
So we need to make an arrangement.


00:12:53.297 --> 00:12:54.840
COLE:
There's a set of bylaws...


00:12:55.048 --> 00:12:58.176
...posted right outside the door here
of this very saloon.


00:12:58.385 --> 00:13:01.597
<i>Your boys do like the bylaws say,
everything will be muy bueno.</i>


00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:06.143
- And if they don't?
COLE: I arrest them.


00:13:06.602 --> 00:13:11.398
- And if they don't go along?
- I shoot them, or Mr. Hitch does.


00:13:11.565 --> 00:13:13.358
- That's the law.
- Your law.


00:13:13.567 --> 00:13:15.193
The same thing.


00:13:17.404 --> 00:13:18.739
Hm.


00:13:21.533 --> 00:13:23.201
Maybe you aren't good enough.


00:13:25.704 --> 00:13:28.165
Don't be so sure you're quicker than me.


00:13:28.373 --> 00:13:30.709
So far I've been quick enough.


00:13:40.844 --> 00:13:42.346
Well...


00:13:43.138 --> 00:13:45.724
...perhaps now is not the time.


00:13:47.851 --> 00:13:50.520
Don't mean there won't be a time.


00:13:52.064 --> 00:13:54.900
COLE:
See you and your boys there are heeled.


00:13:55.108 --> 00:13:57.861
I know you haven't had a chance
to read the bylaws yet...


00:13:58.028 --> 00:14:01.156
...but the bylaws say it's illegaI
to carry guns inside town limits.


00:14:01.323 --> 00:14:04.701
So next time I'm gonna have to disarm you,
lock you up for a bit.


00:14:07.537 --> 00:14:08.872
[CHUCKLES]


00:14:10.916 --> 00:14:13.752
You are an interesting man, Mr. Cole.


00:14:17.506 --> 00:14:19.091
Come on.


00:14:29.351 --> 00:14:32.437
Mr. Cole's been doing this
a long time, Mr. Olson.


00:14:32.646 --> 00:14:35.649
Oh, yeah, ahem. Thank you.


00:14:36.817 --> 00:14:39.945
- Good day to you.
- Good day, Mr. Olson.


00:14:52.332 --> 00:14:54.293
[TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING]


00:15:20.027 --> 00:15:22.654
- Thank you, that'll be fine. I'll be back.
- Yes, ma'am.


00:16:37.604 --> 00:16:41.066
Coffee and a biscuit, please.


00:16:41.275 --> 00:16:42.943
No sell.


00:16:43.485 --> 00:16:45.862
- But it's on the menu.
- With breakfast.


00:16:46.029 --> 00:16:47.406
Chin.


00:16:48.031 --> 00:16:50.826
- Sell the lady a biscuit.
- Menu say-


00:16:50.993 --> 00:16:52.995
Sell her a biscuit.


00:16:53.453 --> 00:16:55.247
One time.


00:16:58.208 --> 00:17:00.711
ALLISON: Thank you.
- My pleasure.


00:17:03.505 --> 00:17:05.007
Are you the sheriff around here?


00:17:05.424 --> 00:17:07.217
City marshaI.


00:17:07.384 --> 00:17:09.177
VirgiI Cole.


00:17:09.595 --> 00:17:12.931
Now, this fella here's my deputy,
Everett Hitch.


00:17:13.765 --> 00:17:16.560
- Ma'am.
- How do you do?


00:17:23.317 --> 00:17:24.901
Thank you.


00:17:26.194 --> 00:17:29.156
HITCH: Thanks, Chin.
CHIN: You're welcome.


00:17:37.998 --> 00:17:39.291
[CHUCKLES]


00:17:46.298 --> 00:17:52.471
Excuse me. Could either of you gentlemen
direct me to a clean, inexpensive hoteI?


00:17:52.679 --> 00:17:56.183
- We only have one.
- Is it expensive?


00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:59.645
COLE: Probably more than it should be,
there being no other choice.


00:17:59.853 --> 00:18:01.480
I only have a dollar.


00:18:02.356 --> 00:18:03.690
Do you have a name?


00:18:04.232 --> 00:18:06.109
Mrs. French.


00:18:07.361 --> 00:18:08.904
Allison French.


00:18:11.365 --> 00:18:12.950
Thank you.


00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:19.248
Uh, you have a husband, Mrs. French?


00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.083
He died.


00:18:22.376 --> 00:18:24.336
I'm sorry to hear that.


00:18:25.754 --> 00:18:27.506
You do any kind of work?


00:18:27.673 --> 00:18:30.008
I play the organ and the piano.


00:18:30.175 --> 00:18:31.385
You're not a whore?


00:18:34.221 --> 00:18:35.973
- What?
- Don't be crude.


00:18:36.139 --> 00:18:38.350
Well, no sense
fluffing your feathers about it.


00:18:38.517 --> 00:18:41.186
We don't see a lot of single women here
that ain't whores.


00:18:41.353 --> 00:18:42.521
Well, I'm one.


00:18:42.729 --> 00:18:44.898
Sprightly thing.


00:18:46.483 --> 00:18:49.194
ALLISON: Do you think the hoteI
will let me stay for a dollar?


00:18:49.361 --> 00:18:52.364
You can stay as long as you like,
Mrs. French.


00:18:53.407 --> 00:18:56.493
- Now, how can that be?
- Might even hire you to play the piano.


00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:58.954
- Think so, Everett?
- I do.


00:19:02.165 --> 00:19:03.542
Well...


00:19:08.922 --> 00:19:10.549
When you finish your breakfast...


00:19:10.757 --> 00:19:13.969
...Everett will escort you down to the hoteI
and help you get settled.


00:19:14.136 --> 00:19:15.470
It'll be my pleasure.


00:19:16.722 --> 00:19:19.182
Thank you very much, Mr. Cole.


00:19:20.392 --> 00:19:22.769
- For your kindness.
- No trouble at all.


00:19:24.896 --> 00:19:29.901
- Hope to see you again, Mrs. French.
- Yes, Mr. Cole. That would be nice.


00:19:48.337 --> 00:19:50.505
You been gone a while.


00:19:53.091 --> 00:19:55.761
She was asking a lot about you, VirgiI.


00:20:28.085 --> 00:20:31.797
Well, was she asking in a liking way?


00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.220
- Wanted to know if you were married.
- Well, what'd you tell her?


00:20:38.387 --> 00:20:39.972
Said I didn't know.


00:20:40.681 --> 00:20:42.891
Well, hell, Everett,
you see a wife around here?


00:20:43.058 --> 00:20:44.101
I do not.


00:20:44.268 --> 00:20:46.603
Then why the hell did you tell her
you didn't know?


00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:50.899
You might have a wife in Silver City.
Or in Nogales. Or Bisbee.


00:20:51.066 --> 00:20:55.487
Bisbee? Everett, if I had a wife in Bisbee,
don't you think you'd know about her?


00:20:56.154 --> 00:21:00.909
Allie says she's gonna ask you about it,
so you might wanna have an answer ready.


00:21:02.703 --> 00:21:05.539
I had an Apache woman
come live with me once...


00:21:05.706 --> 00:21:08.500
...but there were never any words
spoke over us or anything.


00:21:08.667 --> 00:21:11.128
I think she wants to know-
She's more interested...


00:21:11.336 --> 00:21:12.921
...in if you're presently married.


00:21:13.088 --> 00:21:15.090
Well, hell no, I'm not presently married.


00:21:15.257 --> 00:21:17.509
She's gonna be pleased.


00:21:23.473 --> 00:21:25.017
Allie?


00:21:27.019 --> 00:21:31.106
Yes, Allie. She likes to be called Allie.


00:21:38.822 --> 00:21:40.616
So, what do you think?


00:21:41.366 --> 00:21:44.870
I think Mrs. French- Allie.


00:21:45.078 --> 00:21:47.706
- might become exclusively interesting.


00:21:47.873 --> 00:21:50.709
I mean, what do you think
about the men on the ridge?


00:21:53.045 --> 00:21:56.548
I think you and me might wanna
ride up there, see what they're doing.


00:21:57.758 --> 00:21:59.635
Can I finish my coffee first?


00:21:59.801 --> 00:22:01.803
You surely may.


00:22:09.937 --> 00:22:11.855
Howdy, boys.


00:22:14.441 --> 00:22:16.735
Town don't come out this far, marshaI.


00:22:16.944 --> 00:22:18.403
By God, I believe you're right.


00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:20.697
I believe it ends
at the bottom of that hill...


00:22:20.864 --> 00:22:21.949
...where that wash runs.


00:22:22.115 --> 00:22:25.035
Up here,
you're just another cowboy with a gun.


00:22:25.202 --> 00:22:26.662
You think that's right, Everett?


00:22:26.828 --> 00:22:30.415
I think no matter where you are,
you're not just another cowboy with a gun.


00:22:30.624 --> 00:22:31.750
That'd be my thought.


00:22:31.959 --> 00:22:36.255
Well, we ain't doing nothing wrong,
and you ain't got no "jurdiction" up here.


00:22:37.297 --> 00:22:38.590
"Jurdiction"?


00:22:39.091 --> 00:22:40.634
I believe he means jurisdiction.


00:22:40.801 --> 00:22:44.137
I believe he does,
and he's by God right about it.


00:22:44.304 --> 00:22:46.598
What are you doing
riding round and round up here?


00:22:46.765 --> 00:22:49.017
We're just keeping an eye on things.


00:22:49.184 --> 00:22:50.811
For who?


00:22:50.978 --> 00:22:52.271
[CHUCKLES]


00:22:52.437 --> 00:22:53.438
[GRUNTING]


00:22:58.527 --> 00:22:59.861
Ow!


00:23:00.487 --> 00:23:01.613
You knocked my teeth out.


00:23:01.822 --> 00:23:05.450
Well, Colt makes a heavy firearm.
That's a fact.


00:23:05.867 --> 00:23:07.953
Who are you riding for?


00:23:08.370 --> 00:23:10.080
Bragg.


00:23:10.330 --> 00:23:13.458
- Think Bragg's attempting to frighten us?
- Be my guess.


00:23:13.625 --> 00:23:14.751
What's your name?


00:23:14.918 --> 00:23:15.961
- Dean.
- Well, Dean...


00:23:16.128 --> 00:23:19.047
...go back to Mr. Bragg
and report that we ain't too frightened.


00:23:19.214 --> 00:23:21.592
Mr. Bragg ain't gonna like
that you hit me.


00:23:21.758 --> 00:23:25.012
I don't guess you liked it
all that much yourself, Dean.


00:23:25.178 --> 00:23:29.099
- You're damn right.
- So you and Mr. Bragg can commi-


00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:32.519
- What word am I trying for?
- Commiserate?


00:23:32.686 --> 00:23:36.231
You and Mr. Bragg
can commiserate each other.


00:23:36.898 --> 00:23:39.401
You son of a bitch.


00:23:39.568 --> 00:23:40.736
[PIANO PLAYING]


00:23:40.902 --> 00:23:43.530
COLE: Hard to believe Jack Bell
got himself killed.


00:23:46.533 --> 00:23:49.369
Well, what do you think happened
between him and Bragg?


00:23:51.246 --> 00:23:53.999
- Overconfident?
- Be my surmise.


00:23:54.458 --> 00:23:55.834
Mm-hm.


00:23:56.043 --> 00:23:59.671
COLE: Probably thought Bragg
had some respect for the law.


00:23:59.838 --> 00:24:01.089
Mm-hm.


00:24:01.256 --> 00:24:03.216
Ain't just gunplay.
You know that, Everett.


00:24:03.383 --> 00:24:05.928
You gotta think about men too.


00:24:07.721 --> 00:24:11.516
Guess that'd be one reason you're here
and Jack Bell isn't.


00:24:11.725 --> 00:24:15.270
Well, that'd be one reason.
You'd be another.


00:24:28.158 --> 00:24:30.160
[CHATTERING]


00:24:31.787 --> 00:24:34.122
Mighty fine piano playing. Mighty fine.


00:24:34.289 --> 00:24:36.291
Why, thank you.


00:24:38.418 --> 00:24:40.629
- Thank you. Oh, that's plenty.
- Little bit more?


00:24:40.796 --> 00:24:42.714
It's plenty, it's plenty.


00:24:42.923 --> 00:24:44.758
Thank you.


00:24:53.684 --> 00:24:56.186
- To music.
- To music.


00:25:03.610 --> 00:25:05.612
So tell me, Mr. Cole-


00:25:05.779 --> 00:25:07.948
- Call me VirgiI.
- Of course, VirgiI.


00:25:08.115 --> 00:25:11.410
How long have you been killing people
for a living?


00:25:11.952 --> 00:25:15.998
Well, Allie, I don't kill people for a living.


00:25:16.164 --> 00:25:18.250
I enforce the law.


00:25:18.417 --> 00:25:21.962
Killing's sometimes
a sort of side thing of that.


00:25:22.129 --> 00:25:25.215
That's not what I wanted to say.
What am I aiming at here, Everett?


00:25:25.382 --> 00:25:28.468
- Byproduct.
- Killing's sometimes a byproduct.


00:25:28.885 --> 00:25:31.430
And you've never killed anyone
except as a lawman?


00:25:31.638 --> 00:25:33.265
Never.


00:25:33.473 --> 00:25:35.642
Is he telling me the truth, Everett?


00:25:35.809 --> 00:25:37.436
VirgiI always tells the truth.


00:25:37.603 --> 00:25:39.980
Oh, nobody always tells the truth.


00:25:40.147 --> 00:25:43.150
- Why not?
- Well, they...


00:25:43.525 --> 00:25:45.944
For heaven's sake, VirgiI, they just don't.


00:25:46.111 --> 00:25:49.698
Always thought the truth was simpler.
Tell a man what you mean.


00:25:50.115 --> 00:25:51.742
And a woman?


00:25:53.035 --> 00:25:56.455
- A woman?
- That's what I said.


00:25:58.081 --> 00:26:03.629
Well, Allie, I don't really remember
ever telling a woman anything.


00:26:03.795 --> 00:26:05.130
VirgiI Cole.


00:26:05.297 --> 00:26:07.090
[CHUCKLING]


00:26:07.257 --> 00:26:08.634
What?


00:26:08.800 --> 00:26:12.179
Are you telling me
that you've never had a woman?


00:26:12.846 --> 00:26:16.642
Well, hell, Allie, I don't think that's
something I should be discussing with you.


00:26:16.808 --> 00:26:18.977
- But have you?
- Well, of course I have.


00:26:20.145 --> 00:26:22.147
And did you never tell them anything?


00:26:24.358 --> 00:26:27.361
Mostly, we just did
what we were there to do.


00:26:28.362 --> 00:26:30.530
Which was what?


00:26:33.575 --> 00:26:36.328
We won't talk about this anymore.


00:26:39.122 --> 00:26:41.333
Oh, VirgiI.


00:26:43.168 --> 00:26:46.213
- I was just funning you.
- I didn't enjoy it.


00:26:46.380 --> 00:26:48.674
MAN 1:
Shit. Damn you.


00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:50.425
Two more, Wallis.


00:26:50.592 --> 00:26:53.345
You scrawny little bastard,
where are you putting it all?


00:26:53.512 --> 00:26:54.596
Hell, you ain't even pissed.


00:26:54.763 --> 00:26:56.848
MAN 2: I can outdrink you
any day of the week.


00:26:57.057 --> 00:27:00.185
MAN 1: Say when, Wallis.
WALLIS: When.


00:27:01.103 --> 00:27:02.562
[LAUGHING]


00:27:02.729 --> 00:27:05.107
Shit. Shit.


00:27:08.568 --> 00:27:10.821
- Shut up.
MAN 1: What's that, marshaI?


00:27:10.988 --> 00:27:13.532
- Get out of here.
- We ain't doing anything.


00:27:14.157 --> 00:27:16.159
[GRUNTING]


00:27:21.039 --> 00:27:22.708
HITCH:
No, VirgiI.


00:27:22.874 --> 00:27:26.003
VirgiI! VirgiI!


00:27:27.629 --> 00:27:29.256
Quit it!


00:27:32.217 --> 00:27:33.760
VirgiI.


00:27:34.886 --> 00:27:35.887
VirgiI.


00:27:38.599 --> 00:27:40.392
You can let go.


00:27:47.316 --> 00:27:49.276
You can let go.


00:28:13.592 --> 00:28:15.594
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:28:17.679 --> 00:28:20.766
Mr. Hitch,
may I have a word with you, please, sir?


00:28:20.933 --> 00:28:22.184
HITCH:
Certainly.


00:28:22.351 --> 00:28:26.563
Mr. Hitch, it's about the teamster
that Mr. Cole, uh...


00:28:26.730 --> 00:28:29.107
Well, the teamster he busted up was-


00:28:29.274 --> 00:28:32.110
Well, no, is a city employee, sir.


00:28:32.319 --> 00:28:34.613
- You might wanna take that up with VirgiI.
- Uh, yeah.


00:28:34.780 --> 00:28:37.950
Well, I thought you might be
more approachable.


00:28:38.158 --> 00:28:40.494
You know, more amenable.


00:28:40.661 --> 00:28:43.413
We can't have law officers
beating people half to death...


00:28:43.580 --> 00:28:44.748
...for no good reason.


00:28:44.915 --> 00:28:48.335
I took a bottle of whiskey to Tub
this morning, told him VirgiI was sorry.


00:28:48.502 --> 00:28:50.921
Well, perhaps he should have
taken it there himself.


00:28:51.088 --> 00:28:53.507
VirgiI doesn't do things like that.


00:28:53.674 --> 00:28:57.261
Well, what he did, sir, was crazy.


00:28:57.427 --> 00:29:01.056
- You calling VirgiI crazy?
- Yes. No. Uh...


00:29:01.223 --> 00:29:02.266
Well, if-


00:29:02.432 --> 00:29:05.143
You think a man makes a living
as a gun hand isn't crazy?


00:29:05.352 --> 00:29:08.981
- You're not crazy.
- Maybe. Maybe not.


00:29:09.564 --> 00:29:11.858
Whatever I am, I'm not VirgiI Cole.


00:29:12.025 --> 00:29:14.653
It doesn't give him the right
to bust up innocent people.


00:29:14.861 --> 00:29:15.862
No, it doesn't.


00:29:16.029 --> 00:29:18.031
Mostly, innocent people
don't get busted up.


00:29:18.198 --> 00:29:20.325
If they do,
it's because of who and what VirgiI is.


00:29:20.534 --> 00:29:23.870
And you hired him to be VirgiI Cole.


00:29:24.246 --> 00:29:26.999
I'm not sure I understand.


00:29:27.791 --> 00:29:29.126
No.


00:29:29.876 --> 00:29:32.170
I'm not sure you do either.


00:29:32.921 --> 00:29:34.965
- Good day.
- Yes.


00:30:35.275 --> 00:30:36.902
MAN:
Abner.


00:30:57.464 --> 00:30:59.758
- Morning, Abner.
- Morning.


00:31:01.635 --> 00:31:05.722
- Morning, Everett.
- Well, good morning, VirgiI.


00:31:08.183 --> 00:31:11.311
- Morning, Tilda.
- Morning, Mr. Cole.


00:31:15.065 --> 00:31:16.483
Thank you.


00:31:27.160 --> 00:31:30.122
- Everything good with you and Allie?
- Lovely.


00:31:30.289 --> 00:31:34.293
She is a lovely woman,
and everything's lovely between us.


00:31:34.501 --> 00:31:36.712
Well, I'm glad to hear it.


00:31:41.967 --> 00:31:45.137
- Good morning, Everett.
- Morning.


00:31:50.058 --> 00:31:51.852
Thank you.


00:31:55.731 --> 00:31:57.357
There you are.


00:31:58.066 --> 00:31:59.651
Thank you.


00:32:03.322 --> 00:32:04.990
Guess what, Everett?


00:32:05.198 --> 00:32:06.533
What?


00:32:06.909 --> 00:32:10.162
You know that house that's being built
on the east end of South Street?


00:32:10.370 --> 00:32:11.371
Uh-huh.


00:32:11.538 --> 00:32:14.666
Well, Mr. Olson was having it built
for his daughter and her husband.


00:32:14.833 --> 00:32:16.668
- Right.
- But they're moving to Virginia.


00:32:17.210 --> 00:32:20.672
- So he's gonna sell it.
- Well...


00:32:21.715 --> 00:32:23.175
To VirgiI and me.


00:32:25.385 --> 00:32:27.638
It's gonna be
the most beautifuI house in town...


00:32:27.804 --> 00:32:30.349
...with a parlor and a white picket fence.


00:32:30.557 --> 00:32:34.019
And a big porch
so we can see who's coming to call.


00:32:36.730 --> 00:32:38.106
Well...


00:32:42.277 --> 00:32:44.112
How about that?


00:32:55.791 --> 00:32:57.292
I ain't- I ain't armed.


00:32:59.086 --> 00:33:00.754
My name is Whitfield.


00:33:00.921 --> 00:33:03.715
I'm Joe Whitfield
and I'm a hand over at Bragg's place.


00:33:08.720 --> 00:33:11.682
Allie, I'm gonna need to talk to this fella
alone for a minute.


00:33:11.848 --> 00:33:13.267
Oh.


00:33:13.600 --> 00:33:15.477
Well, certainly.


00:33:16.186 --> 00:33:19.690
Have to do my piano exercises anyway.


00:33:25.445 --> 00:33:27.573
I was up on the rim
when you and your deputy-


00:33:27.739 --> 00:33:30.284
You came up and smacked Dean.


00:33:33.996 --> 00:33:35.998
I took on because...


00:33:36.707 --> 00:33:39.376
I took on because Bragg
was supposed to be running cattle.


00:33:39.543 --> 00:33:42.170
- And that's what I know.
- What are you driving at, son?


00:33:43.338 --> 00:33:46.425
I was at Bragg's place when MarshaI Bell
and his deputies was killed.


00:33:46.592 --> 00:33:48.468
[PIANO PLAYING IN DISTANCE]


00:33:48.635 --> 00:33:50.429
Who done it?


00:33:51.805 --> 00:33:53.432
Bragg done it.


00:33:56.643 --> 00:33:59.271
You saw Randall Bragg shoot Jack Bell?


00:33:59.438 --> 00:34:01.481
Yes, sir. And his two deputies.


00:34:01.648 --> 00:34:03.984
He shot them all dead
like they was rattlesnakes.


00:34:04.151 --> 00:34:05.903
Sit down there.


00:34:07.237 --> 00:34:08.614
Sit down.


00:34:12.910 --> 00:34:15.662
I don't want no part in killing people.


00:34:16.663 --> 00:34:19.082
You testify to what you saw?


00:34:20.417 --> 00:34:21.793
Yes. Yes, sir.


00:34:21.960 --> 00:34:24.421
- With Bragg looking right at you?
- I will.


00:34:25.714 --> 00:34:28.926
Because we don't wanna go up there,
shoot up a bunch of people...


00:34:29.092 --> 00:34:31.887
...and get Bragg into court
to have you dry up and blow away.


00:34:32.054 --> 00:34:34.139
I'll say what I saw.


00:34:35.140 --> 00:34:37.142
COLE:
Give me your word on that?


00:34:39.102 --> 00:34:40.604
I do.


00:36:18.243 --> 00:36:20.412
You're under arrest
for the murder of Jack Bell.


00:36:20.621 --> 00:36:22.456
Don't make a sound.


00:36:25.042 --> 00:36:28.879
- You can't do this, Cole.
- Yeah, well, I'm doing it.


00:36:29.046 --> 00:36:30.464
HITCH:
Let's go.


00:36:35.010 --> 00:36:36.345
[GUNSHOT]


00:36:43.769 --> 00:36:46.146
Get on your horses. They've got Bragg.


00:36:54.029 --> 00:36:56.031
[MEN SHOUTING]


00:36:59.993 --> 00:37:02.329
Keep that gun on him, Everett.


00:37:03.997 --> 00:37:05.332
MAN:
Come on over there.


00:37:22.766 --> 00:37:26.311
You try anything, you're a dead man.


00:37:27.646 --> 00:37:29.648
VINCE:
What you like us to do, Mr. Bragg?


00:37:29.856 --> 00:37:31.817
COLE:
Tell them to lower their guns.


00:37:33.026 --> 00:37:34.987
Hold off, Vince.


00:37:35.237 --> 00:37:37.197
Lower your guns.


00:37:39.074 --> 00:37:41.034
Lower your guns.


00:38:08.020 --> 00:38:09.771
[HORSES NEIGHING]


00:38:14.568 --> 00:38:17.362
COLE: Tell them not to follow
or I'll blow your jaw off.


00:38:17.529 --> 00:38:19.615
- Vince.
- Yes, sir, Mr. Bragg?


00:38:19.781 --> 00:38:22.242
BRAGG: Don't let them follow,
you understand? Stay put.


00:38:23.076 --> 00:38:24.870
If you say so, Mr. Bragg.


00:38:40.594 --> 00:38:43.138
- Out of the way.
- Stop it.


00:38:48.268 --> 00:38:51.313
- It's Mr. Bragg.
- Yes, it is.


00:38:52.105 --> 00:38:53.106
[CHILDREN CHATTERING]


00:38:53.273 --> 00:38:54.775
They have him well in hand.


00:38:56.610 --> 00:38:59.196
Circuit judge don't come through
for two and a half weeks.


00:38:59.363 --> 00:39:02.783
You're wasting your time, Cole.
You've got no proof.


00:39:15.671 --> 00:39:17.256
You're a dead man.


00:39:18.590 --> 00:39:20.759
HITCH:
That's not very neighborly.


00:39:20.926 --> 00:39:22.636
You're dead.


00:39:29.017 --> 00:39:31.103
You'll never hang me, Cole.


00:39:31.520 --> 00:39:34.481
Never's a long time, Mr. Bragg.


00:39:42.781 --> 00:39:44.908
I'm gonna go check on Allie.


00:39:45.075 --> 00:39:49.037
First sign of any trouble,
fire off a couple rounds, I'll be here.


00:39:49.329 --> 00:39:51.290
Unless you're riding at a hard gallop.


00:39:51.456 --> 00:39:52.624
[CHUCKLES]


00:39:54.334 --> 00:39:57.921
Everett, we've known each other
a long time.


00:39:58.088 --> 00:40:01.300
I don't care for that kind of dis- Dis-


00:40:02.801 --> 00:40:05.470
- Disparaging?
- Disparaging remarks.


00:40:05.637 --> 00:40:06.972
Especially about Allie.


00:40:12.477 --> 00:40:14.563
No, and you shouldn't.


00:40:15.188 --> 00:40:16.773
I apologize.


00:40:16.940 --> 00:40:18.859
You meant no harm.


00:40:19.443 --> 00:40:21.403
Apology accepted.


00:40:37.252 --> 00:40:39.671
I know you're scared, son.


00:40:41.089 --> 00:40:45.344
You keep your word and testify,
I promise we'll get you out of here safely.


00:40:50.182 --> 00:40:51.850
Thank you, sir.


00:40:52.225 --> 00:40:53.852
You're welcome.


00:41:43.110 --> 00:41:46.238
Allie's chewing on me like a young dog.


00:41:46.446 --> 00:41:51.159
Says all I do is be a marshaI,
sit around minding our prisoner.


00:41:51.326 --> 00:41:53.287
That I care more about marshaling
than her.


00:41:53.453 --> 00:41:56.707
That I ain't even brung you down
to see the house yet.


00:41:58.292 --> 00:42:00.460
I was figuring to see it
when it's all finished.


00:42:00.627 --> 00:42:02.671
Well, go on down there, will you?


00:42:02.838 --> 00:42:04.590
Calm her down a little.


00:42:04.798 --> 00:42:07.509
You know, tell her you like it.


00:42:09.303 --> 00:42:10.345
What do you got there?


00:42:10.512 --> 00:42:14.433
She asked me which one I liked
for the curtain.


00:42:14.600 --> 00:42:15.601
Mm-hm.


00:42:15.809 --> 00:42:19.313
Everett, I ain't- I never owned a house.
I didn't know what to say to her.


00:42:19.896 --> 00:42:23.483
If the wind picks up, house'll blow down
and you won't have to worry about it.


00:42:23.650 --> 00:42:27.112
That house ain't going nowhere.
I got a carpenter that used to build boats.


00:42:27.321 --> 00:42:30.824
Will you go on down there, please?
Go on.


00:42:30.991 --> 00:42:33.493
Just- You know,
she's planning the furniture.


00:42:33.660 --> 00:42:35.037
All right.


00:42:35.203 --> 00:42:36.788
Here, take these with you.


00:42:36.955 --> 00:42:40.000
Tell her she can pick
whichever one she likes.


00:42:41.460 --> 00:42:44.171
You know, I'm kind of partiaI
to this one here, but look.


00:42:44.338 --> 00:42:47.132
Look at that.
You can see right through it.


00:42:50.677 --> 00:42:53.305
Kind of small for curtains, aren't they?


00:42:54.097 --> 00:42:56.141
Get on down there.


00:43:16.745 --> 00:43:18.580
Everett.


00:43:19.039 --> 00:43:21.041
Afternoon, Allie.


00:43:21.875 --> 00:43:23.877
I must look awfuI.


00:43:24.044 --> 00:43:28.215
- You look lovely. Always do.
- You're too kind, Everett.


00:43:29.716 --> 00:43:32.594
VirgiI said you should
pick out the curtains.


00:43:33.679 --> 00:43:36.014
Couldn't make up his mind.


00:43:38.225 --> 00:43:39.768
House is hurrying right along.


00:43:39.935 --> 00:43:43.021
VirgiI ever decides to come and live in it.


00:43:43.480 --> 00:43:45.190
Pretty sure he will.


00:43:45.399 --> 00:43:47.568
Doesn't pay any attention to the house.


00:43:47.734 --> 00:43:51.071
Hell, Everett,
he doesn't pay any attention to me.


00:43:51.863 --> 00:43:56.326
Just sits up in his jaiI with his gun...


00:43:56.493 --> 00:43:58.328
...being the marshaI.


00:43:59.037 --> 00:44:03.417
Well, has been somewhat expectant
of late.


00:44:03.959 --> 00:44:06.336
Yeah, but it's his job.


00:44:06.503 --> 00:44:08.547
It's not his life.


00:44:12.467 --> 00:44:15.971
- Yeah.
- It'll be so elegant.


00:44:16.179 --> 00:44:17.848
Come see.


00:44:18.557 --> 00:44:19.683
This is the parlor...


00:44:19.850 --> 00:44:24.062
...so we can look out
and see everybody who's coming to call.


00:44:26.273 --> 00:44:28.817
Come and see this. Come and see.


00:44:29.067 --> 00:44:33.155
That will be the bedroom,
and this will be the kitchen.


00:44:33.488 --> 00:44:36.074
And you'll come often to visit us?


00:44:36.491 --> 00:44:37.951
Every time I'm invited.


00:44:38.118 --> 00:44:40.454
I can cook, you know.


00:44:41.705 --> 00:44:43.749
I never imagined you couldn't.


00:44:53.091 --> 00:44:55.260
Do you think I'm pretty?


00:44:56.261 --> 00:44:58.263
Well, yes.


00:45:13.862 --> 00:45:16.990
Allie, you're with VirgiI.


00:45:17.241 --> 00:45:18.367
So am I.


00:45:20.035 --> 00:45:22.287
VirgiI's not here.


00:45:25.832 --> 00:45:28.168
We're not with each other.


00:45:29.836 --> 00:45:31.713
We're both with him.


00:45:34.174 --> 00:45:36.051
Let go of me.


00:45:36.969 --> 00:45:40.347
- Do you understand what I'm saying?
- Let go.


00:45:40.514 --> 00:45:42.808
- Allie.
- Let go.


00:45:52.401 --> 00:45:54.319
Just leave.


00:46:16.425 --> 00:46:18.427
[HOOFBEATS IN DISTANCE]


00:46:34.192 --> 00:46:36.194
- We come for Mr. Bragg.
COLE: You can't have him.


00:46:36.361 --> 00:46:39.364
Everett, step on in the office
with that eight-gauge.


00:46:39.531 --> 00:46:42.200
First anything happens,
you blow Mr. Bragg's head off.


00:46:42.367 --> 00:46:44.745
- Yes, sir.
- We'll take him if we have to.


00:46:44.912 --> 00:46:46.204
If you do, he'll be dead.


00:46:49.207 --> 00:46:52.169
We know you're good, Cole,
but you're not as good as 20 of us.


00:46:52.336 --> 00:46:53.879
COLE:
You know the arrangement, boy.


00:46:54.254 --> 00:46:56.214
First one of you
does an ineluctable thing-


00:46:56.423 --> 00:46:58.550
VINCE: You shoot him,
you think we're gonna ride away?


00:46:58.717 --> 00:46:59.801
Nope.


00:47:00.928 --> 00:47:03.221
- We'll kill you and Hitch.
- You'll try.


00:47:03.430 --> 00:47:05.682
You're willing to die
to keep us from taking him?


00:47:05.849 --> 00:47:07.392
COLE:
Sure.


00:47:08.644 --> 00:47:10.646
Hitch. You willing to die too?


00:47:10.812 --> 00:47:15.400
Of course he's willing to die. You think
we do this because we're scared to die?


00:47:16.109 --> 00:47:17.653
HITCH:
You got them turned.


00:47:18.111 --> 00:47:19.780
They're arguing with him.


00:47:20.197 --> 00:47:21.657
COLE:
You?


00:47:21.949 --> 00:47:22.950
Me?


00:47:23.617 --> 00:47:25.118
You afraid to die?


00:47:25.577 --> 00:47:28.956
- I ain't afraid.
- Good, because you go first.


00:47:29.581 --> 00:47:32.501
And that boy with the red scarf
goes next.


00:47:37.130 --> 00:47:38.799
You go on home, Vince.


00:47:39.841 --> 00:47:41.843
You go on home.


00:47:42.594 --> 00:47:44.763
Go on. Too many people die if you don't.


00:47:46.348 --> 00:47:47.808
Go on. Get on.


00:47:47.975 --> 00:47:50.769
Go. Get. All of you, get out of here.


00:47:50.936 --> 00:47:53.814
- There'll be another time, Cole.
COLE: Get out of here, get. Hyah!


00:47:54.231 --> 00:47:55.566
Hyah!


00:47:57.317 --> 00:47:59.069
ALLISON:
VirgiI?


00:48:02.281 --> 00:48:05.367
- Are you all right?
- Yeah, I'm all right, Allie.


00:48:06.201 --> 00:48:08.120
Let's get you inside.


00:48:14.334 --> 00:48:16.128
What did you do?


00:48:18.171 --> 00:48:21.174
- What do you care?
- What did you do?


00:48:27.723 --> 00:48:29.182
I ran off.


00:48:29.349 --> 00:48:30.642
[CHUCKLES]


00:48:33.186 --> 00:48:36.189
- You say anything to Mr. Cole?
- No.


00:48:36.356 --> 00:48:38.942
- You gonna say anything?
- No.


00:48:40.319 --> 00:48:42.696
VirgiI couldn't hear a thing like that.


00:48:46.700 --> 00:48:49.202
I don't want him hearing about it
from you either.


00:48:49.369 --> 00:48:52.205
He finds out, I'll know
who couldn't keep her mouth closed.


00:48:53.707 --> 00:48:58.045
There have been a few times
when you didn't want my mouth closed.


00:49:07.220 --> 00:49:10.682
What if she tells him
and says it was your doing?


00:49:12.893 --> 00:49:14.519
Why would she do that?


00:49:15.103 --> 00:49:17.272
Sooner or later she's gonna tell him.


00:49:30.077 --> 00:49:33.997
HITCH: Good morning, Tilda.
- Morning, Mr. Hitch.


00:49:40.921 --> 00:49:43.507
Couldn't help but notice your books,
marshaI.


00:49:45.592 --> 00:49:48.136
What's the fascination with Emerson?


00:49:49.054 --> 00:49:52.975
Not the most elegant writer,
but he gets his point across.


00:49:55.143 --> 00:49:58.730
Though I'm sure the layman
is sometimes a little befuddled...


00:49:58.897 --> 00:50:03.402
...by his obfuscating vocabulary,
wouldn't you say?


00:50:03.610 --> 00:50:05.362
We've been treating you kindly, Bragg.


00:50:05.529 --> 00:50:07.864
In return, we expect you
to speak when spoken to...


00:50:08.031 --> 00:50:10.075
...and otherwise keep your mouth shut.


00:50:10.659 --> 00:50:12.119
I can speak if I want to.


00:50:12.286 --> 00:50:14.830
VirgiI and I can beat
the sweet Jesus hell out of you...


00:50:14.997 --> 00:50:17.874
...every morning for breakfast
if we want to.


00:50:28.635 --> 00:50:32.973
Clyde Stringer, county sheriff.
My undersheriff, Charlie Tewksbury.


00:50:33.140 --> 00:50:34.891
- VirgiI Cole?
- Right there.


00:50:35.058 --> 00:50:37.269
Been expecting you, sheriff.


00:50:37.853 --> 00:50:39.313
Clyde.


00:50:39.897 --> 00:50:40.939
- Charlie.
- Morning.


00:50:41.106 --> 00:50:42.983
This fella's my deputy, Everett Hitch.


00:50:43.150 --> 00:50:47.029
We just came in on a train from Yaqui
with Judge Elias Callison.


00:50:47.362 --> 00:50:52.117
This fella here's our witness.
Former hand of Bragg, Joe Whitfield.


00:50:52.451 --> 00:50:54.786
- You're gonna testify?
- Yes, sir.


00:50:54.953 --> 00:50:58.624
- If he doesn't die of fright first.
- We been keeping him seque-


00:50:59.833 --> 00:51:00.834
Seq-


00:51:03.128 --> 00:51:05.380
S- Seq-


00:51:06.256 --> 00:51:08.300
What's the word I'm looking for?


00:51:08.467 --> 00:51:12.387
- Sequestered.
COLE: Sequestered here for safety.


00:51:14.139 --> 00:51:17.351
Charlie and I'd be happy to help
till the triaI's over if you need it.


00:51:17.517 --> 00:51:19.811
Might just take you boys up on that.


00:51:21.647 --> 00:51:23.732
- Good morning.
- Good morning, gentlemen.


00:51:23.899 --> 00:51:25.317
RAINES:
Going for a little buggy ride?


00:51:25.484 --> 00:51:29.488
Yeah, me and Mrs. French
are gonna do a little perambulating.


00:51:31.323 --> 00:51:33.200
HITCH:
Mr. Raines, Mr. May.


00:51:33.367 --> 00:51:35.244
RAINES:
Morning, Everett.


00:51:35.410 --> 00:51:37.204
Got your goodies.


00:51:39.039 --> 00:51:42.000
- Sure you can handle this rig?
- Well...


00:51:45.754 --> 00:51:47.339
You know them?


00:51:48.090 --> 00:51:50.175
COLE:
The Shelton brothers.


00:51:50.342 --> 00:51:52.844
HITCH: They do law work?
COLE: They do gun work.


00:51:53.387 --> 00:51:56.014
- They good?
- They're excellent.


00:51:56.473 --> 00:51:58.100
Good as you and me?


00:51:58.267 --> 00:52:00.394
Don't know that they ain't.


00:52:01.562 --> 00:52:03.272
Don't appear to be heeled.


00:52:07.401 --> 00:52:09.027
Well...


00:52:11.196 --> 00:52:13.031
It's been a long time, VirgiI.


00:52:14.741 --> 00:52:17.703
- Ring.
- You remember my brother?


00:52:17.869 --> 00:52:19.663
COLE: Mackie.
- VirgiI.


00:52:19.830 --> 00:52:21.290
Can I buy you a drink?


00:52:23.417 --> 00:52:25.377
Are you still doing that?


00:52:25.836 --> 00:52:27.379
Well, we ain't.


00:52:27.588 --> 00:52:29.548
[CHUCKLING]


00:52:31.133 --> 00:52:32.884
This is my deputy, Everett Hitch.


00:52:33.051 --> 00:52:35.012
You as good as VirgiI with a gun?


00:52:35.178 --> 00:52:37.431
I never seen anybody as good as VirgiI.


00:52:38.015 --> 00:52:41.727
- But you ain't saying you ain't as good.
- Not discussing it, truth be told.


00:52:41.893 --> 00:52:43.687
What are you and Mackie doing in town?


00:52:43.854 --> 00:52:46.648
Everybody's gotta be somewhere,
don't they, Mackie?


00:52:46.815 --> 00:52:50.903
You got a triaI coming up, a big one.
Might wanna take that in.


00:52:51.904 --> 00:52:53.405
I like a good triaI.


00:52:53.614 --> 00:52:55.365
ALLISON:
Good morning.


00:52:58.660 --> 00:52:59.828
This is Mrs. French.


00:53:01.288 --> 00:53:02.789
Ma'am.


00:53:03.707 --> 00:53:04.917
Gentlemen.


00:53:08.462 --> 00:53:10.088
Thank you.


00:53:12.716 --> 00:53:15.969
Well, you boys been in my towns before.


00:53:17.054 --> 00:53:19.139
You know the rules.


00:53:20.223 --> 00:53:21.642
Come on.


00:53:22.601 --> 00:53:24.770
Haven't done this for a while.


00:53:27.022 --> 00:53:30.525
I always figured VirgiI
for whores and squaws.


00:53:32.611 --> 00:53:33.654
She's neither.


00:53:34.488 --> 00:53:36.281
I'll be damned.


00:53:36.782 --> 00:53:38.116
[MACKIE GRUNTS]


00:53:39.159 --> 00:53:41.161
[ALLISON LAUGHING IN DISTANCE]


00:53:43.664 --> 00:53:44.998
COLE:
We can try if you wanna.


00:53:45.415 --> 00:53:47.459
What happened next?


00:53:58.887 --> 00:54:01.515
Mr. Bragg shot the deputy dead
with his Winchester.


00:54:01.682 --> 00:54:03.308
You're a goddamn liar!


00:54:03.475 --> 00:54:05.143
[GASPING AND CHATTERING]


00:54:08.689 --> 00:54:10.983
One more outburst
such as that, Mr. Bragg...


00:54:11.149 --> 00:54:14.695
...and I will give Sheriff Stringer
the authority to shut you up...


00:54:14.861 --> 00:54:16.655
...in any manner he sees fit.


00:54:16.822 --> 00:54:20.659
With all due respect, Your Honor,
my client's life is on the line.


00:54:20.826 --> 00:54:23.412
His life is not on the line yet, counselor.


00:54:25.080 --> 00:54:28.542
He'll have his chance to speak. Sit down.


00:54:29.042 --> 00:54:31.044
Go ahead, son.


00:54:33.338 --> 00:54:37.926
Then Mr. Bragg shot MarshaI Bell
and his other deputy.


00:54:38.093 --> 00:54:39.386
[CHATTERING]


00:54:39.595 --> 00:54:42.806
You saw this happen
with your own eyes, son?


00:54:42.973 --> 00:54:44.516
Yes, sir.


00:54:46.435 --> 00:54:48.353
Thank you, Mr. Whitfield.


00:54:48.520 --> 00:54:50.898
Mr. Mueller,
you may cross-examine the witness.


00:54:57.195 --> 00:55:00.741
<i>WALLIS: You swear to tell the whole truth
and nothing but the truth, so help you God?</i>


00:55:00.908 --> 00:55:01.950
<i>VINCE:
I do.</i>


00:55:06.830 --> 00:55:10.250
Well, Mr. Sullivan,
what have you got to say for yourself?


00:55:10.792 --> 00:55:14.713
Jack Bell and his deputies
never came up to Mr. Bragg's ranch.


00:55:14.880 --> 00:55:16.882
I don't know
what Whitfield's talking about.


00:55:17.049 --> 00:55:19.051
That's the same thing
all of you have said.


00:55:20.719 --> 00:55:23.805
Does anybody have
anything different to say other than:


00:55:23.972 --> 00:55:27.517
"Jack Bell and his deputies
never came up to Mr. Bragg's ranch...


00:55:27.684 --> 00:55:30.103
...and I don't know
what Whitfield's talking about"?


00:55:33.607 --> 00:55:35.692
You may step down.


00:55:36.902 --> 00:55:41.073
Well, no reason to waste time
saying the same thing over and over again.


00:55:41.281 --> 00:55:43.659
MUELLER: My client has a right to testify
in his own defense.


00:55:43.825 --> 00:55:46.411
CALLISON:
Of course he does. One moment.


00:55:46.578 --> 00:55:47.913
Mr. Whitfield...


00:55:49.373 --> 00:55:50.540
...do you own a horse?


00:55:50.707 --> 00:55:51.917
Yes. Yes, sir.


00:55:52.125 --> 00:55:54.711
Well, son, I suggest
while the bees are in the butter...


00:55:54.878 --> 00:55:57.631
...you get on your horse and ride.


00:55:57.798 --> 00:55:59.925
Ride and don't look back.


00:56:01.260 --> 00:56:04.763
- Now.
MAN: Ride hard, boy. Ride hard.


00:56:12.312 --> 00:56:13.730
CALLISON:
Swear him in, Mr. Wallis.


00:56:17.526 --> 00:56:19.528
Put your hand on the Bible.


00:56:19.945 --> 00:56:22.447
- Do you swear to tell the whole truth-
- I swear.


00:56:22.614 --> 00:56:24.449
- so help you God?


00:56:26.827 --> 00:56:30.289
Your Honor,
I sense a certain antipathy toward-


00:56:30.497 --> 00:56:32.666
Sit down, Mr. Bragg.


00:56:33.834 --> 00:56:36.169
I sense a certain antipathy
toward me here today...


00:56:36.336 --> 00:56:38.964
...because I'm a relative newcomer.


00:56:40.048 --> 00:56:44.261
Now, I didn't kill Jack Bell or his deputies.
Jack was a friend of mine.


00:56:44.428 --> 00:56:45.804
I had no reason to kill him.


00:56:46.972 --> 00:56:51.351
Mr. Whitfield is nothing more
than a fearfuI boy...


00:56:51.518 --> 00:56:54.980
...easily persuaded to say anything.


00:56:55.147 --> 00:56:58.066
Easily persuaded by MarshaI Cole.


00:56:58.567 --> 00:57:00.527
Now, the citizens of Appaloosa...


00:57:01.028 --> 00:57:04.990
...have allowed Mr. Cole
to take over their town.


00:57:05.824 --> 00:57:10.203
But it is not justice
in this new nation of ours...


00:57:10.412 --> 00:57:14.374
...to allow him to deprive me
of my liberty...


00:57:14.708 --> 00:57:18.337
...let alone my life.


00:57:21.048 --> 00:57:23.550
Eloquent, Mr. Bragg.


00:57:24.843 --> 00:57:27.054
But unconvincing.


00:57:27.554 --> 00:57:29.514
I find you guilty of these charges...


00:57:29.681 --> 00:57:31.058
[CROWD CHATTERING]


00:57:31.224 --> 00:57:33.685
...and sentence you to hang
at Yaqui Prison.


00:57:36.563 --> 00:57:37.689
Court's adjourned.


00:57:58.710 --> 00:58:00.212
Everett?


00:58:02.256 --> 00:58:05.968
"What I must do is all that concerns me...


00:58:06.134 --> 00:58:08.595
...not what the people think.


00:58:09.888 --> 00:58:16.562
This rule, equally arduous
in actuaI and in intellectuaI life... "


00:58:18.564 --> 00:58:20.190
Arduous.


00:58:36.039 --> 00:58:39.084
We'll bring out sourdough and ham
when we get to Chester.


00:58:39.251 --> 00:58:40.836
How long till Chester?


00:58:42.629 --> 00:58:44.631
Three quarters of an hour.


00:58:46.049 --> 00:58:50.012
When we reach the upgrade,
you'll feeI the train slow down.


00:58:50.178 --> 00:58:53.140
Ain't a hell of a grade,
but it's a long one.


00:58:54.141 --> 00:58:56.143
[TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING]


00:59:04.192 --> 00:59:07.279
- We're just gonna take a look outside.
- I got him.


01:00:06.922 --> 01:00:09.091
So you see how this is gonna go.


01:00:11.218 --> 01:00:14.263
Any sign of trouble from anyone
and Mackie gives her both barrels.


01:00:14.680 --> 01:00:18.684
Or she breaks her neck
and is dragged through the mesquite.


01:00:19.226 --> 01:00:21.478
So you folks
are gonna have to unshackle Bragg...


01:00:21.645 --> 01:00:25.023
...and parade him on out here
or she gets killed.


01:00:25.190 --> 01:00:27.192
STRINGER:
I got you in my sights.


01:00:27.359 --> 01:00:30.237
Whatever happens to her, you're dead.


01:00:36.910 --> 01:00:40.998
What do you think, VirgiI? You think
I'm gonna get scared and change my mind?


01:01:02.644 --> 01:01:04.104
Put your rifle down.


01:01:04.271 --> 01:01:05.731
STRINGER: Sorry, Cole,
this ain't your jurisdiction.


01:01:05.898 --> 01:01:07.524
Put it down!


01:01:07.691 --> 01:01:08.775
You too, Everett.


01:01:15.991 --> 01:01:17.492
Charlie.


01:01:22.039 --> 01:01:25.375
We give you Bragg,
you give us the woman.


01:01:25.542 --> 01:01:27.794
VirgiI, you know I ain't that dumb.


01:01:27.961 --> 01:01:31.048
You give us Bragg, we keep the woman.
You ride off on that train...


01:01:31.214 --> 01:01:34.635
...and when you're out of sight,
we'll cut her loose.


01:01:43.477 --> 01:01:44.978
Give them Bragg.


01:01:45.395 --> 01:01:47.314
Charlie, go get him.


01:02:07.417 --> 01:02:09.628
- Give me a gun!
RING: No.


01:02:09.795 --> 01:02:12.881
- I'm gonna shoot that son of a bitch.
RING: That ain't part of the deaI.


01:02:13.048 --> 01:02:15.133
Damn it, Ring, I hired you. Give me a gun.


01:02:15.342 --> 01:02:16.718
RING:
You owe me money.


01:02:16.885 --> 01:02:19.137
UntiI you pay me,
you ain't getting no gun.


01:02:22.849 --> 01:02:25.143
Move on up the track.


01:02:25.686 --> 01:02:27.813
I told you you'd never hang me, Cole.


01:02:27.980 --> 01:02:29.481
Never ain't here yet.


01:03:36.465 --> 01:03:38.550
HITCH:
Leave him be, sheriff.


01:03:40.218 --> 01:03:43.889
But we got no horses.
We can't chase him on foot.


01:03:45.307 --> 01:03:48.101
We'll go on back to Appaloosa
and get some.


01:03:49.269 --> 01:03:52.731
The quicker Cole gets back here,
the quicker we can get out of here.


01:03:52.981 --> 01:03:54.775
He won't come back.


01:03:55.943 --> 01:03:57.694
STRINGER:
Won't come back?


01:03:58.362 --> 01:04:01.198
Nope. He won't come back.


01:04:14.503 --> 01:04:17.089
We've got no horses, VirgiI.


01:04:19.258 --> 01:04:22.135
I'll ride the train back to town
and fetch them.


01:04:22.302 --> 01:04:25.264
You stray off the wash, leave me a sign.


01:05:16.440 --> 01:05:18.817
Well, by God.


01:05:20.027 --> 01:05:22.738
- VirgiI.
- Everett.


01:05:24.072 --> 01:05:25.657
You bring any coffee?


01:05:26.366 --> 01:05:27.993
Done so.


01:06:15.582 --> 01:06:17.292
You all right?


01:06:19.002 --> 01:06:20.837
All right?


01:06:21.421 --> 01:06:23.173
Well, how do you feeI?


01:06:23.340 --> 01:06:25.342
About Allie and all.


01:06:27.886 --> 01:06:29.388
Everett...


01:06:30.597 --> 01:06:33.100
...we've been together now a while.


01:06:33.267 --> 01:06:36.478
Can't exactly say how long, but long.


01:06:36.728 --> 01:06:39.856
Ain't anybody
I'd rather do this work with.


01:06:40.190 --> 01:06:45.612
You're as good as anybody I've seen,
except maybe the Shelton boys and me.


01:06:46.321 --> 01:06:51.410
The reason you ain't as good
as the Sheltons or me...


01:06:51.618 --> 01:06:55.831
...ain't got nothing to do
with steady or fast or fortuitous.


01:06:56.123 --> 01:07:00.752
The reason the above-named folks are
better than you is because you got feelings.


01:07:01.503 --> 01:07:04.089
Well, hell, VirgiI,
everybody's got feelings.


01:07:04.298 --> 01:07:06.550
Feelings get you killed.


01:07:07.968 --> 01:07:10.971
You got feelings about Allie, don't you?


01:07:11.680 --> 01:07:16.268
I cared about Allie in town,
and I'll care about her when I get her back.


01:07:19.646 --> 01:07:24.693
But right now there's something running,
and we're trying to catch it.


01:07:46.506 --> 01:07:48.258
There they are.


01:07:48.842 --> 01:07:50.510
HITCH:
Yeah, I see them.


01:07:55.390 --> 01:07:56.975
COLE:
Yup, that's Allie.


01:07:57.142 --> 01:07:59.811
Hey, Virg, look north.


01:08:00.103 --> 01:08:01.396
Up on the flats.


01:08:07.527 --> 01:08:08.654
Chiricahua, I reckon.


01:08:08.820 --> 01:08:13.158
Probably broke out of San Carlos,
headed down to Mexico.


01:08:15.202 --> 01:08:18.288
COLE: Looks like they stole horses.
A lot of them ain't Indians' ponies.


01:08:18.455 --> 01:08:20.624
HITCH:
Pretty raggedy-looking bunch.


01:08:20.874 --> 01:08:23.210
They will be a problem.


01:08:23.585 --> 01:08:25.837
I speculate they will.


01:09:01.915 --> 01:09:04.001
COLE:
You see Allie anywhere?


01:09:10.799 --> 01:09:12.134
HITCH: Yes, I do.
ALLISON: Whoo!


01:09:12.301 --> 01:09:13.552
[RING LAUGHING]


01:09:14.678 --> 01:09:16.263
What is it?


01:09:19.016 --> 01:09:20.684
Give me that thing.


01:09:50.130 --> 01:09:51.173
There's Bragg.


01:09:56.637 --> 01:09:58.639
ALLISON:
Are you sure about that?


01:10:06.063 --> 01:10:07.231
HITCH:
I think about 10 of them.


01:10:07.397 --> 01:10:10.317
COLE: We start shooting, they'll scatter.
Won't know how many we are.


01:10:10.484 --> 01:10:12.194
HITCH:
Won't go far.


01:10:12.653 --> 01:10:15.447
A lot of stuff they want down there.


01:10:16.156 --> 01:10:18.116
[WHOOPING]


01:10:22.371 --> 01:10:23.956
[MAN SPEAKING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]


01:10:40.764 --> 01:10:44.017
ALLISON:
No. Oh, no, no. No, stop!


01:10:44.601 --> 01:10:47.396
RING: Hey.
ALLISON: No! No!


01:10:48.021 --> 01:10:49.690
Ring!


01:10:49.982 --> 01:10:52.234
- No!
COLE: Shoot the packhorse.


01:10:52.401 --> 01:10:53.485
[GUNSHOT]


01:10:55.529 --> 01:10:56.905
[GUNSHOTS]


01:10:57.698 --> 01:10:59.741
[GUNSHOTS]


01:11:00.867 --> 01:11:02.202
[GUNSHOTS]


01:11:06.582 --> 01:11:08.166
COLE:
Hey, whoa.


01:11:09.334 --> 01:11:11.837
- Get away from there.
- Get out of there.


01:11:14.715 --> 01:11:16.633
Where do you think you're going?


01:11:17.009 --> 01:11:18.844
- Back behind the tree.
- VirgiI.


01:11:19.011 --> 01:11:21.138
COLE:
You too, Allie.


01:11:21.597 --> 01:11:24.975
Everett, get the bags off that packhorse.


01:11:31.940 --> 01:11:33.400
RING:
I knew you'd be coming after us.


01:11:34.276 --> 01:11:36.236
Oh, you did, huh?


01:11:38.530 --> 01:11:40.115
Where you headed?


01:11:40.282 --> 01:11:43.160
Little town, Rio Seco, two days' ride.


01:11:43.368 --> 01:11:45.120
COLE: While we got these hostiles
to deaI with...


01:11:45.287 --> 01:11:47.247
...ain't a good idea
us shooting each other.


01:11:47.831 --> 01:11:51.168
I say we put our troubles aside
till we get there.


01:11:51.418 --> 01:11:52.419
Your word?


01:11:53.420 --> 01:11:55.172
My word.


01:11:55.422 --> 01:11:56.798
COLE:
Mackie?


01:11:56.965 --> 01:11:58.926
My word, Cole.


01:11:59.468 --> 01:12:01.428
Give them their guns, Everett.


01:12:05.182 --> 01:12:09.269
Mackie, you got some clothes in there,
cover Allie up?


01:12:12.773 --> 01:12:14.316
ALLISON:
Thank you.


01:12:17.194 --> 01:12:19.655
They've seen pretty much
everything you got, Allie.


01:12:19.821 --> 01:12:22.115
No sense hiding it now.


01:12:25.118 --> 01:12:27.037
We'll dig in here. Keep watch.


01:12:27.204 --> 01:12:29.831
Mackie, get up on that hillside there
somewhere.


01:12:30.249 --> 01:12:34.878
Everett, soon as Ring gets his boots on,
have a look either end of this canyon.


01:12:37.631 --> 01:12:40.259
Good to see you again, Mr. Bragg.


01:14:13.060 --> 01:14:15.938
VirgiI, how do we know
they're still there?


01:14:17.898 --> 01:14:19.733
COLE:
Oh, they're still there, Allie.


01:14:26.531 --> 01:14:29.159
RING:
What the hell these son of bitches doing?


01:14:32.246 --> 01:14:34.414
What the hell
do you think they're gonna do?


01:14:34.581 --> 01:14:36.583
BRAGG:
I'll tell you what they're gonna do.


01:14:36.750 --> 01:14:39.169
- They're gonna wait untiI our food's gone.
- Shut up.


01:14:39.336 --> 01:14:41.880
BRAGG: They're gonna wait
untiI we're beat down with the heat.


01:14:42.047 --> 01:14:44.758
About the time they smell the blood
of stock that you've killed...


01:14:44.925 --> 01:14:47.469
- ... because you're starving to death-
- I said shut up.


01:14:47.636 --> 01:14:49.388
I'm gonna ride up and see.


01:14:49.596 --> 01:14:50.764
BRAGG:
Hey.


01:14:50.931 --> 01:14:53.767
Where the hell do you think you're going
with my horse?


01:16:31.740 --> 01:16:33.742
[THUNDER RUMBLING]


01:18:15.219 --> 01:18:19.139
- Bragg owes me money.
- He's my prisoner.


01:18:20.474 --> 01:18:22.809
He stays my prisoner.


01:18:23.518 --> 01:18:26.104
You're taking this personaI, VirgiI.


01:18:29.441 --> 01:18:33.820
When we get to Rio Seco,
we'll take care of the business between us.


01:18:36.698 --> 01:18:39.201
Everett, let's go spell Mackie.


01:18:43.330 --> 01:18:44.873
Come on.


01:18:54.633 --> 01:18:56.176
ALLISON:
VirgiI?


01:18:57.010 --> 01:18:58.845
Yes, Allie?


01:19:00.681 --> 01:19:03.350
ALLISON: Can I come up
and sit with you and Everett?


01:19:03.934 --> 01:19:05.102
Come on.


01:19:05.727 --> 01:19:07.729
[RUSTLING AND FOOTSTEPS]


01:19:29.626 --> 01:19:31.920
I'm sorry, VirgiI.


01:19:34.590 --> 01:19:36.466
Stay here, Everett.


01:19:40.220 --> 01:19:42.055
ALLISON:
I'm sorry.


01:19:42.598 --> 01:19:46.351
I was so alone, and Bragg...


01:19:47.227 --> 01:19:50.188
Well, Ring protected me
and so did his brother.


01:19:50.397 --> 01:19:53.358
- You fuck Mackie too?
- No.


01:19:54.026 --> 01:19:57.779
It was Ring. He was in charge.


01:20:03.243 --> 01:20:06.204
I just did what I had to do.


01:20:06.830 --> 01:20:08.373
Everett...


01:20:08.874 --> 01:20:13.170
...Ring kills me,
do you think she'll go off with him?


01:20:23.263 --> 01:20:27.726
I think Allie needs to be with a man.


01:20:27.935 --> 01:20:30.270
You're a bastard.


01:20:31.480 --> 01:20:32.522
Don't listen to him.


01:20:32.689 --> 01:20:36.318
He tried to put his hands on me
when I showed him our house.


01:20:36.902 --> 01:20:40.405
No, VirgiI. I did not.


01:20:41.156 --> 01:20:45.827
No, Allie. Everett didn't do that.


01:20:48.413 --> 01:20:51.959
- You believe him over me?
- That's correct.


01:20:53.752 --> 01:20:55.420
Yeah.


01:21:18.402 --> 01:21:20.404
[CHATTERING]


01:21:38.589 --> 01:21:41.675
I'm VirgiI Cole, marshaI of Appaloosa.


01:21:41.842 --> 01:21:43.969
This is my deputy, Everett Hitch.


01:21:45.679 --> 01:21:48.807
These are the Shelton boys.
This man here is my prisoner.


01:21:48.974 --> 01:21:52.561
He's been sentenced to hang in Yaqui
for the murder of a city marshaI.


01:21:53.145 --> 01:21:58.317
I need him, uh, sequestered for a spell
while I get a few things in order.


01:22:01.320 --> 01:22:03.655
By all means, marshaI.


01:22:04.489 --> 01:22:06.366
Appreciate it.


01:22:13.415 --> 01:22:16.752
How do I know you ain't gonna
try to collect Bragg and skedaddle?


01:22:16.919 --> 01:22:20.714
You've known me a long time, Ring.
Long as I've known you.


01:22:21.340 --> 01:22:23.342
[BELL TOLLING]


01:22:23.508 --> 01:22:25.177
Two hours.


01:22:25.719 --> 01:22:27.596
Stockyards.


01:22:27.971 --> 01:22:29.765
I'll be there.


01:22:35.479 --> 01:22:37.189
COLE:
Come on, Allie.


01:22:39.483 --> 01:22:41.693
HITCH:
Kind of hard not to kiss her back a little...


01:22:43.028 --> 01:22:45.864
...seeing's her lips were on mine.


01:22:49.701 --> 01:22:51.870
But I held her off.


01:22:52.287 --> 01:22:54.706
Told her we weren't with each other.


01:22:54.873 --> 01:22:56.875
We were both with you.


01:22:58.085 --> 01:23:01.171
She didn't care for it. Got kind of fitfuI.


01:23:07.761 --> 01:23:10.097
I never met a woman like her.


01:23:12.599 --> 01:23:18.313
Mostly I've been with whores
and that squaw lady I told you about.


01:23:21.066 --> 01:23:25.279
She speaks well and dresses fine...


01:23:25.696 --> 01:23:27.823
...and she's good-looking...


01:23:28.615 --> 01:23:31.785
...she can play the piano,
and she cooks good...


01:23:31.952 --> 01:23:34.121
...and she's very clean.


01:23:35.581 --> 01:23:38.041
Chews her food nice.


01:23:40.961 --> 01:23:45.591
But it appears she'll fuck anything
ain't gelded.


01:23:45.799 --> 01:23:49.386
I'm not certain that's quite right.


01:23:49.553 --> 01:23:51.513
What do you think's right?


01:23:52.222 --> 01:23:54.474
I think she wants to be
with the boss stallion.


01:23:54.641 --> 01:23:56.643
There's only one stallion in a herd.


01:23:57.060 --> 01:23:58.270
At a time.


01:23:58.729 --> 01:24:00.063
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]


01:24:09.907 --> 01:24:11.909
[SPEAKING IN SPANISH]


01:24:20.626 --> 01:24:23.253
So when I'm around, she loves me.


01:24:23.420 --> 01:24:25.213
I think so.


01:24:26.340 --> 01:24:29.134
When I'm not around, she loves you.


01:24:29.301 --> 01:24:30.636
Well, it's probably not love.


01:24:30.802 --> 01:24:33.222
When neither one of us is around,
she loves Ring.


01:24:33.388 --> 01:24:37.059
Again, not so sure I'd say love.


01:24:39.394 --> 01:24:41.188
She love me?


01:24:42.856 --> 01:24:44.483
What do you think?


01:24:47.402 --> 01:24:49.321
I think she does.


01:24:49.488 --> 01:24:51.657
You're the one should know.


01:24:54.159 --> 01:24:58.121
You know she takes a bath every evening
before she goes to bed?


01:25:00.332 --> 01:25:02.376
I like being with her.


01:25:02.709 --> 01:25:04.711
Nothing against it.


01:25:06.088 --> 01:25:08.090
Just gotta get past this Ring business.


01:25:09.007 --> 01:25:12.135
- Might not be the last time for that.
- It'll be the last time with Ring.


01:25:12.302 --> 01:25:14.304
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]


01:25:15.472 --> 01:25:16.557
ALLISON:
It's me.


01:25:19.601 --> 01:25:21.478
Come in, Allie.


01:25:29.570 --> 01:25:31.572
[CHUCKLING]


01:25:33.657 --> 01:25:36.702
Well, it's all the hoteI keeper could find.


01:25:36.910 --> 01:25:39.246
You look lovely, Allie.


01:25:39.580 --> 01:25:41.290
Truly.


01:25:54.636 --> 01:25:56.722
Aren't either of you afraid?


01:25:58.098 --> 01:25:59.099
Afraid?


01:26:00.225 --> 01:26:02.102
That you might get killed?


01:26:03.687 --> 01:26:05.731
Oh, I don't know, Allie.


01:26:07.774 --> 01:26:10.485
Guess I don't think about it so much.


01:26:12.362 --> 01:26:13.614
Well, I'm afraid.


01:26:16.825 --> 01:26:18.785
But I'm afraid all the time.


01:26:22.080 --> 01:26:23.081
Of what?


01:26:24.625 --> 01:26:25.667
Everything.


01:26:26.335 --> 01:26:28.086
Like what?


01:26:31.506 --> 01:26:32.758
Hm?


01:26:34.218 --> 01:26:36.428
Like being alone.


01:26:37.054 --> 01:26:38.805
Like being with the wrong man.


01:26:38.972 --> 01:26:41.266
Not having any money...


01:26:41.642 --> 01:26:43.769
...a place to live.


01:26:52.277 --> 01:26:54.029
I'II look out for you.


01:26:58.909 --> 01:27:00.619
For how long?


01:27:01.161 --> 01:27:03.372
For as long as you need.


01:27:12.631 --> 01:27:15.300
We've done pretty well over time, VirgiI.


01:27:15.467 --> 01:27:19.513
It's always been just a job.
Never been personaI.


01:27:22.349 --> 01:27:25.310
We are going up against Ring
because of Bragg, right?


01:27:25.477 --> 01:27:29.314
You can't be a lawman
and let somebody take your prisoner.


01:27:36.238 --> 01:27:38.240
[BELL TOLLING]


01:27:46.248 --> 01:27:47.833
RING:
Cole!


01:27:52.754 --> 01:27:57.050
Like you said, you've known me
a long time, long as I've known you.


01:28:01.054 --> 01:28:03.098
Guess you made your first mistake,
VirgiI...


01:28:03.265 --> 01:28:06.602
...locking your prisoner
in my cousin Russell's jaiI.


01:28:10.731 --> 01:28:14.276
COLE: I'll take Ring, you take Mackie,
then we'll deaI upstairs.


01:28:14.443 --> 01:28:15.944
Yes, sir.


01:28:32.252 --> 01:28:33.587
[HORSE NEIGHS]


01:28:44.056 --> 01:28:46.058
[GRUNTING]


01:28:47.351 --> 01:28:48.894
VirgiI.


01:28:52.981 --> 01:28:54.483
VirgiI.


01:28:55.484 --> 01:28:56.735
VirgiI.


01:28:57.945 --> 01:29:00.530
Left knee's busted.


01:29:03.575 --> 01:29:07.621
HITCH: That happened quick.
- Everybody could shoot.


01:29:13.710 --> 01:29:15.295
ALLISON:
VirgiI.


01:29:17.798 --> 01:29:19.424
VirgiI.


01:29:20.300 --> 01:29:21.843
VirgiI.


01:29:22.427 --> 01:29:23.929
Allie.


01:29:30.811 --> 01:29:36.191
And I want you to know
how embarrassed I am that you saw me...


01:29:36.775 --> 01:29:38.110
- You know.
- What?


01:29:38.277 --> 01:29:41.113
I am mortified that you saw me
with no clothes on.


01:29:41.280 --> 01:29:43.824
Oh, Allie,
it was an incomparable pleasure.


01:29:43.991 --> 01:29:45.242
Oh, Everett.


01:29:45.409 --> 01:29:47.744
Well, you're the one
that started talking about it.


01:29:47.911 --> 01:29:52.374
Well, I'm just gratefuI to you and Everett
that you didn't abandon me.


01:29:52.541 --> 01:29:54.376
Well, that is what we were hired to do.


01:29:54.543 --> 01:29:58.088
You know, find escaped prisoners
and rescue damsels in distress.


01:29:58.255 --> 01:30:00.799
Oh, go on, the both of you.


01:30:00.966 --> 01:30:04.803
Pretend like you were just doing
what any lawman would do.


01:30:05.012 --> 01:30:08.765
I know it in my heart and I treasure it...


01:30:08.932 --> 01:30:11.602
...that you did what you did for me.


01:30:17.107 --> 01:30:19.484
KATIE:
That's what I was trying to say.


01:30:20.068 --> 01:30:22.863
Allie has you in reserve.


01:30:23.363 --> 01:30:27.326
- In reserve for what?
- Everett, you ain't stupid.


01:30:27.492 --> 01:30:31.622
VirgiI dies, you replace him.


01:30:33.290 --> 01:30:37.377
- No.
- That's why she's so nice to you.


01:30:39.129 --> 01:30:41.715
You don't think she loves VirgiI?


01:30:44.718 --> 01:30:48.013
Out here, love's pretty hard for a woman.


01:30:48.180 --> 01:30:51.058
Mostly it's the men worry about love.


01:30:51.266 --> 01:30:52.559
I don't know what she feels.


01:30:52.726 --> 01:30:56.396
She probably don't know
how she feels either.


01:30:56.563 --> 01:31:01.610
She just knows he's the top hand,
and she'll stay with him till he ain't.


01:31:10.911 --> 01:31:13.413
Hello, Everett. Hello, VirgiI.


01:31:13.580 --> 01:31:15.082
What can we do for you boys?


01:31:15.249 --> 01:31:21.171
Well, there's a been a strange,
somewhat of an odd occurrence.


01:31:21.463 --> 01:31:22.798
COLE:
Occurrence?


01:31:22.965 --> 01:31:26.552
Just came in from the telegraph office
minutes ago.


01:31:26.760 --> 01:31:29.012
It's from Judge Callison.


01:31:42.109 --> 01:31:45.946
"Have received notice
from U.S. Department of Justice.


01:31:46.113 --> 01:31:48.949
Randall R. Bragg granted full pardon...


01:31:49.116 --> 01:31:52.452
...for murder conviction
in Yaqui County...


01:31:52.619 --> 01:31:54.871
...by President Chester A. Arthur. "


01:31:55.038 --> 01:32:00.294
Evidently, Bragg's claim of association
with our president wasn't just thrasonicaI.


01:32:00.460 --> 01:32:01.795
[MUTTERS]


01:32:04.631 --> 01:32:06.341
BoastfuI.


01:32:14.516 --> 01:32:15.809
Thank you, gentlemen.


01:32:15.976 --> 01:32:17.895
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


01:32:18.061 --> 01:32:20.397
Why did you just thrust that
in his face like that?


01:32:20.564 --> 01:32:23.108
- I didn't.
- You thrusted it in his face.


01:32:24.568 --> 01:32:27.321
COLE: Thanks, Tilda.
- Mr. Cole.


01:32:29.489 --> 01:32:31.658
- I'll trade you-
- I know what you're gonna ask.


01:32:31.825 --> 01:32:33.952
- Here.
- Do you want my drumstick too?


01:32:34.119 --> 01:32:36.288
No. One's plenty.


01:32:36.496 --> 01:32:37.497
I knew it.


01:32:37.664 --> 01:32:39.666
[DOOR CREAKS AND FOOTSTEPS]


01:32:39.833 --> 01:32:42.127
Well, by God.


01:32:50.010 --> 01:32:51.678
Mrs. French.


01:32:52.262 --> 01:32:53.847
MarshaI. Deputy.


01:32:59.186 --> 01:33:02.439
- Bygones be bygones.
- Bragg...


01:33:03.649 --> 01:33:06.318
...I don't know what kind of deaI
you worked...


01:33:06.735 --> 01:33:10.197
...but as far as I'm concerned,
you murdered Jack Bell.


01:33:11.698 --> 01:33:14.368
Now you're standing here
while I'm trying to have dinner...


01:33:14.534 --> 01:33:16.078
...acting like you didn't.


01:33:16.995 --> 01:33:19.873
Well, I'm sorry you feeI that way.


01:33:21.416 --> 01:33:23.252
Mrs. French.


01:33:24.878 --> 01:33:26.505
Everett.


01:33:32.427 --> 01:33:33.971
Gentlemen.


01:33:34.137 --> 01:33:37.182
RAINES:
Mr. Bragg. It's very nice to see you.


01:33:37.391 --> 01:33:39.226
[CHATTERING]


01:33:39.393 --> 01:33:41.895
Why do you think he came back here?


01:33:46.108 --> 01:33:47.734
Pride.


01:33:49.069 --> 01:33:51.321
It's a funny thing, Allie.


01:33:57.869 --> 01:33:59.413
Everett.


01:33:59.913 --> 01:34:01.164
HITCH:
Good trip?


01:34:01.331 --> 01:34:04.251
Well, Judge Callison says
there ain't nothing can be done.


01:34:04.418 --> 01:34:07.629
Bragg's attorney appealed the conviction,
said the triaI was unfair...


01:34:07.796 --> 01:34:10.257
...no bodies were found,
evidence was hearsay.


01:34:10.424 --> 01:34:13.635
President granted a pardon
before the appeaI was even ruled on.


01:34:13.802 --> 01:34:18.599
He's got authority over the territories.
The pardon is reaI. It's the law.


01:34:19.641 --> 01:34:21.268
How's Allie?


01:34:21.935 --> 01:34:23.520
She's fine.


01:34:31.361 --> 01:34:35.908
VirgiI, I've always thought that men like us
do gun work because we can.


01:34:37.200 --> 01:34:39.828
Because we're better at it than most.


01:34:40.037 --> 01:34:43.790
Well, it beats punching cows
or digging copper.


01:34:43.957 --> 01:34:46.293
- Yeah.
- Or soldiering.


01:34:46.877 --> 01:34:49.671
You can do it as a peace officer,
get paid regularly...


01:34:49.838 --> 01:34:52.049
...and you sort of know
when to do it and how.


01:34:52.216 --> 01:34:53.842
Sounds right.


01:34:57.262 --> 01:35:01.975
Never taken the legaI side of it
too seriously.


01:35:03.352 --> 01:35:07.814
I mean, figure it's just a way
to feeI easier about being a gunman.


01:35:07.981 --> 01:35:12.402
I take it serious.
What the hell am I if I don't?


01:35:15.530 --> 01:35:17.532
[PEOPLE CHATTERING
AND PIANO PLAYING]


01:35:32.047 --> 01:35:34.841
MAN 1:
I tell you, this town is changing fast.


01:35:35.008 --> 01:35:37.719
MAN 2:
That's a fine-looking sign.


01:35:37.886 --> 01:35:39.388
MAN 1:
Yup.


01:35:46.019 --> 01:35:47.980
MAN 3: Just send me the bill.
WOMAN: I will.


01:35:48.146 --> 01:35:49.815
MAN 3:
Okay.


01:35:51.567 --> 01:35:53.777
MAN 4:
Here's to you, Dixie.


01:35:59.616 --> 01:36:01.577
Buy you a drink, Everett?


01:36:01.743 --> 01:36:03.328
Got one.


01:36:04.204 --> 01:36:07.916
I'll have the same, Fat.
And a pretty little glass of sherry.


01:36:08.542 --> 01:36:10.335
So where's your partner?


01:36:10.502 --> 01:36:13.088
He refuses to come in here.


01:36:13.422 --> 01:36:16.133
That's fine, perfectly fine.


01:36:17.050 --> 01:36:18.510
Cigar?


01:36:18.677 --> 01:36:20.596
Don't smoke.


01:36:23.473 --> 01:36:27.895
Listen, I understand
why you boys hold it hard against me.


01:36:28.395 --> 01:36:31.857
But I want you to know
I'm not the man I was.


01:36:34.735 --> 01:36:36.737
I was hoping we could work together...


01:36:36.904 --> 01:36:40.032
...once you came to see
the truth of my statement.


01:36:40.866 --> 01:36:43.452
That statement being
that you're a reformed man?


01:36:43.619 --> 01:36:45.329
I am.


01:36:46.538 --> 01:36:49.583
The city aldermen
like what's happening to the town.


01:36:49.875 --> 01:36:53.795
You boys don't get
on the right side of things, well...


01:36:54.129 --> 01:36:57.216
...you might find yourselves
without a job.


01:36:58.592 --> 01:36:59.885
How are we doing here?


01:37:00.052 --> 01:37:02.012
[CHATTERING]


01:37:02.346 --> 01:37:05.974
Losing money, are you?
Don't lose the hoteI in one night.


01:37:06.141 --> 01:37:09.186
Here we are, Allie.
Something to warm you up a little bit.


01:37:09.353 --> 01:37:12.564
- Well, thank you, Randall.
- Sitting lonely in the corner...


01:37:12.731 --> 01:37:13.732
Aw.


01:37:13.941 --> 01:37:15.984
- ... poured into that dress.
- Oh, ha-ha-ha.


01:37:18.946 --> 01:37:21.198
HITCH:
Ever seen one like that?


01:37:21.698 --> 01:37:25.077
Olson says Bragg bought it in England.


01:37:25.369 --> 01:37:27.412
A Herefordshire, they call it.


01:37:27.621 --> 01:37:29.248
That is a fine beast.


01:37:29.456 --> 01:37:32.084
HITCH:
Those steers make reaI good eating.


01:37:34.294 --> 01:37:39.550
One fella told me the other day
Bragg had a big silver strike up in Nevada.


01:37:42.219 --> 01:37:46.640
Another swears Bragg and some boys
robbed a train down in Mexico...


01:37:46.807 --> 01:37:48.934
...carrying gold.


01:37:52.771 --> 01:37:57.109
I don't suppose it matters one way
or the other where he got all that money.


01:37:57.859 --> 01:38:00.445
Must be something can be done.


01:38:04.074 --> 01:38:06.743
They ain't gonna run me off.


01:38:09.913 --> 01:38:13.959
And Bragg's got Olson and his bunch
right in his pocket.


01:38:17.087 --> 01:38:19.798
We got hired. We can get fired.


01:38:19.965 --> 01:38:22.509
Me and Allie got a house here.


01:38:24.011 --> 01:38:25.929
I'm not leaving.


01:38:29.016 --> 01:38:31.268
What are you gonna stay as?


01:38:31.852 --> 01:38:34.104
We ain't come to that yet.


01:38:36.398 --> 01:38:39.860
Might just make some sense to move on.


01:38:44.197 --> 01:38:46.491
Talked this over with Allie?


01:38:47.326 --> 01:38:49.369
She don't wanna leave either?


01:39:09.765 --> 01:39:12.559
I got some things to say, VirgiI.


01:39:18.774 --> 01:39:21.693
I stay here,
I won't be able to make a living.


01:39:22.694 --> 01:39:23.779
I know.


01:39:28.367 --> 01:39:31.995
- I got something else to say.
- She might leave me.


01:39:34.539 --> 01:39:35.874
Yeah.


01:39:36.917 --> 01:39:41.296
- You saw how it was with Ring Shelton.
- I ain't leaving her.


01:39:54.268 --> 01:39:55.769
All right.


01:40:00.774 --> 01:40:02.150
All right.


01:42:38.015 --> 01:42:41.852
I shot a man in Tres Piedras years ago.


01:42:43.770 --> 01:42:46.565
Only time I killed it wasn't legaI.


01:43:20.974 --> 01:43:23.060
I'm gonna be leaving.


01:43:36.657 --> 01:43:39.159
TILDA:
More coffee, Mr. Raines?


01:43:40.494 --> 01:43:43.330
- Will there be anything else for you?
- No, thank you.


01:43:53.507 --> 01:43:55.634
HITCH:
Give this to Bragg when he asks for it.


01:43:55.801 --> 01:43:58.554
- Everett.
- Just do it.


01:43:58.720 --> 01:43:59.805
BRAGG:
Long notes.


01:43:59.972 --> 01:44:01.640
- Yes.
- Yeah?


01:44:01.807 --> 01:44:03.016
[CHATTERING AND LAUGHING]


01:44:04.685 --> 01:44:06.186
Everett.


01:44:08.855 --> 01:44:10.816
What the hell do you think you're doing?


01:44:11.400 --> 01:44:15.195
You're a Iying, back-shooting,
cowardly son of a bitch.


01:44:16.572 --> 01:44:18.365
BRAGG:
What is this?


01:44:19.408 --> 01:44:21.326
What is this?


01:44:21.493 --> 01:44:23.245
I'll be out in the street.


01:44:23.412 --> 01:44:26.832
BRAGG: But you're a deputy marshaI.
You can't call me out.


01:44:27.374 --> 01:44:29.251
Wallis has a gun for you.


01:44:29.418 --> 01:44:32.921
I'm going outside. You don't come out,
I'll come back in and kill you.


01:44:37.676 --> 01:44:41.263
You think you can pull on me
without your friend Cole to back you up?


01:45:00.616 --> 01:45:02.117
Everett.


01:45:02.743 --> 01:45:04.870
Just leave it, VirgiI.


01:45:05.037 --> 01:45:07.497
Just hold on. What's this about?


01:45:08.707 --> 01:45:11.084
I ever ask you for anything?


01:45:12.920 --> 01:45:14.129
Well, I'm asking you now.


01:45:16.256 --> 01:45:18.467
Just leave it alone.


01:45:26.934 --> 01:45:28.769
Just once, VirgiI.


01:45:29.645 --> 01:45:31.438
One favor.


01:47:41.235 --> 01:47:44.071
<i>HITCH: I figured I'd saved Virgil's career
as a lawman...</i>


01:47:45.197 --> 01:47:48.075
<i>...and given him another chance
with Allie.</i>


01:47:48.367 --> 01:47:51.370
<i>At least for the foreseeable future.</i>


01:47:52.412 --> 01:47:53.789
<i>As for the unforeseeable...</i>


01:47:54.706 --> 01:47:58.418
<i>...well, it was out there waiting for me.</i>


01:48:00.379 --> 01:48:05.467
<i>I headed straight into the setting sun
and rode west at an easy pace.</i>


01:48:05.926 --> 01:48:08.220
<i>It was gonna be a long ride...</i>


01:48:08.387 --> 01:48:11.098
<i>...and there was no reason to hurry.</i>

